💜 SkillVerse – Campus Peer-to-Peer Skill Exchange

Learn One. Teach One. Grow Together.

About the Project

SkillVerse is a campus-based peer-to-peer skill exchange platform that helps college students teach skills they already know and learn new skills from other students using virtual SkillCoins.

Problem Statement

Many college students have valuable skills but lack a common platform to share their knowledge and learn from their peers.

Proposed Solution

SkillVerse connects students who want to teach with students who want to learn through a virtual skill-exchange system.

Core Features

- Explore and search available skills.
- Browse skill categories.
- View student mentor profiles.
- Add and manage teaching and learning skills.
- Send and manage exchange requests.
- Virtual SkillCoin wallet.
- Student dashboard and profile.

Technologies and AI Tools

- Google AI Studio
- Generative AI
- Frontend technologies included in the source code
- Local sample data

Development Process

1. Analysed the problem statement.
2. Planned the application features and screens using ChatGPT.
3. Generated the application using Google AI Studio.
4. Tested navigation and interactions.
5. Improved the interface and synchronised the source code with GitHub.

Limitations

This version is a frontend prototype using sample data. Real authentication, shared student accounts, messaging and secure transactions require backend integration.

